# Repo Boundary

## This repo is: a company operating system
Everything in this codebase serves teams and company operations. Brand management, content generation, team workflows, company-level AI features.

## What belongs here
- Company brand context and voice configuration
- AI-powered content generation (social posts, scripts, emails)
- Team management (invites, roles, permissions)
- Company outputs and content library
- External read-only API for trusted consumers
- Any feature a team member or admin would use

## What does NOT belong here
- Personal user features (journals, personal notes, private projects)
- Personal data storage — personal data lives in a separate system (hub-os) with its own database
- Features that only serve a single person rather than a team
- Direct database connections to external systems — use the external API pattern instead

## The boundary test
Before adding a feature, ask: "Would this feature make sense for any company using this product, or is it personal to one individual?"

If it's personal → it belongs in hub-os, not here.
If it's company/team → it belongs here.

## Data boundary
This system has its own Supabase database containing only company data. It never reads from or writes to external databases directly. External systems access company data through the external API (`app/api/external/`).
